  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In given circuit capacitors&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are connected in series , so equivalent capacitance will be&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mstyle></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mstyle></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mstyle></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the switch is closed and capacitors start charged, at time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p>charge on the capacitor is given by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the maximum charge on the capacitor at steady state and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi></math>&nbsp;is the time constant.</p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></math></p><p>Then from the above equation</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mi>E</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mi>E</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Both capacitor will have same charge as they are connected in series<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b27cc1e6-df63-4c7a-aaed-f414647b67fb-image.png\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 180px;\" /></p>",
